config.prompt:
Generate four to six genuinely DIFFERENT framings of this brief, each from a distinct design perspective.

Brief:
{{inputs.brief}}

Constraints:
{{inputs.constraints}}

Different framings, not four wordings of one idea. The point of diverging before committing is that the second option is only useful if it could not have been reached from the first — and a set that agrees with itself gives the evaluator nothing to choose between.

Return JSON: {"framings": [{"lens": string, "sketch": string}]}

Develop the BOLD option, staying inside this lens:
{{nodes.diverge.output.framings}}

Use the first framing. Commit to it — an option that hedges toward the safe answer is the safe answer with extra steps, and the comparison then has nothing to compare.

Brief:
{{inputs.brief}}

Return JSON: {"design": string, "rationale": string, "trade_offs": [string]}

Develop the PRAGMATIC option, staying inside a different lens from option A:
{{nodes.diverge.output.framings}}

Use the second framing. Pragmatic means cheap to build and easy to reverse, not timid — state what it gives up.

Brief:
{{inputs.brief}}

Return JSON: {"design": string, "rationale": string, "trade_offs": [string]}

Choose between these two designs against the constraints, then say what still needs work.

Constraints:
{{inputs.constraints}}

Option A:
{{nodes.option-a.output.design}}
Its trade-offs: {{nodes.option-a.output.trade_offs}}

Option B:
{{nodes.option-b.output.design}}
Its trade-offs: {{nodes.option-b.output.trade_offs}}

You did not write either one, which is the point — pick on the merits and name what the winner costs. A choice presented as free is a choice whose price shows up later.

remaining_issues drives the refinement loop: an empty list ends it. Say empty only when it is true.

Return JSON: {"winner": string, "synthesis": string, "remaining_issues": [string]}

Refine the selected design with a MINIMAL DIFF against the last approved version.

Selected design:
{{nodes.evaluate.output.synthesis}}

Issues to resolve:
{{last.output.remaining_issues}}

Change what the issues require and nothing else. Regenerating the whole design each round loses the parts that were already right, and the reviewer cannot tell what actually changed.

Set issues_resolved true only when remaining_issues is genuinely empty.

Return JSON: {"refined": string, "changed": string, "remaining_issues": [string], "issues_resolved": boolean}
